WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.390
You know, I'm glad you're here, Andy.

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.710
'Cause let's face it, this
is a very strange time.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.445
Very much so, yeah.
It's such a very

00:00:06.445 --> 00:00:08.445
strange time, and it's a confusing time.

00:00:09.378 --> 00:00:11.120
Because during COVID,
we're being bombarded

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.780
with information.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.210
You know, you turn on any TV,

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.320
you go on your computer,

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.350
and they're gonna show you graphs.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.990
Now some of these graphs are important.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.700
But here's what I'm noticing.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.450
A lot of the graphs that
are coming out lately

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.690
don't seem that necessary.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.523
Have you noticed that?

00:00:25.523 --> 00:00:26.570
Absolutely, yeah.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.890
A lot of silly stuff.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:29.080
Yeah, you know?

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.250
For example, I mean, some of these charts

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.610
are, I don't know, they
just seem questionable.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.490
Here's a chart that came out today.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.470
There's apparently been a
huge increase in second naps.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:41.810
Okay.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:46.400
Look at this, there's been a
400% increase in day drinking.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.380
[Andy] I'm drunk now!

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.170
I know, I could tell.
Yeah.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:53.070
That's a good reason to
sit far away from me,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.690
is the smell.
Yeah.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.523
Yeah.

00:00:55.523 --> 00:00:57.140
I got a little closer to you earlier,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.980
and I just smelled bathtub gin.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.420
Yep, yep.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.890
Check this graph out.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.210
There's been a steady increase of

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.860
watching another God damn show on Netflix.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.540
I guess.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.560
Look at this one, this is
not a surprising chart.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.000
But I don't know that we
needed to see this one.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:11.880
Check it out.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.753
Here's the national rate of masturbation.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.870
Okay, is that a chart we needed to see?

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.277
I dunno, I'm kinda getting
off on it. (chuckles)

00:01:22.277 --> 00:01:23.200
I'm kinda getting off on it.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.570
Okay, take it easy.
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:28.187
'Cause you know, the graph is going whoop.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:29.850
All right, all right.
Probably add a little bit

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:30.840
of a slide whistle sound.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.000
Whoop!

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.000
That's, oh, yeah.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.223
Glad you're here!

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.060
It's Randy?

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.710
It can be, I don't care!

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.160
Okay.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.377
Of course, a sharp rise in dads shouting,

00:01:43.377 --> 00:01:45.887
"I used to be a very powerful man!"

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.043
here's the latest graph on time.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.173
Didn't really help me much to see that.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.320
They've also been tracking divorces

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.803
by spouses married to COVID graph makers.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.790
Little meta, but--
Oh boy, that's a sad one.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.430
Yeah, here's an interesting one.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.763
What we talk about with our walls.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.520
There's what's it like being a wall?

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.190
How was your day?

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.890
And wall, you're my only friend.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:16.913
I say that a lot.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.690
Here's a graph I actually
find kinda fascinating.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:23.410
Sharp increase of frat
brothers in Alabama,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:27.090
saying "Oh man, did you hear about Tre?"

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.980
(Andy laughs)

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.350
Tre made a mistake.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.880
Poor Tre.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.560
And finally, given all the other data

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.570
that's out there, here's our last graph.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.833
It's one showing hope.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.860
Always fun to end a comedy
bit on a happy note!

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:44.720
Yeah!

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.660
All right, go out on a bummer!

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.680
Yeah, hey Andy, do me a favor.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.160
Do what our audience back in Burbank

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.310
would usually do.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.650
Oh, all right.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:57.897
It's my birthday!
(Conan laughs)

00:02:57.897 --> 00:02:58.980
I want a hug!

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.810
(Conan laughs)

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.190
(Andy laughs)
Do the string dance!

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:07.231
Yeah, yeah, the T-shirt
cannon broke my teeth!

00:03:07.231 --> 00:03:09.814
(Conan laughs)

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.440
Yep, we do miss our crowds, though.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.273
We do.

00:03:17.273 --> 00:03:19.850
They're some of the
best people in Burbank.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:22.600
(Conan chuckles)

